A few hundred men come from Hamburg; the rest of the Hamburg council talks. On 4 February the Gerstenberg Division storms the city. Dozens die, and the Soviet Republic with them. In Bremen they remember that the Zentrale stood with them.

@strike
subtitle: The Spartacist way: mass action, not a lost battle.
on-arrival: bremen_line = 2; militancy += 4; worker_support += 2; repression += 3; district_bremen_loyalty += 5; luxemburgist_satisfaction += 4; lean_luxemburgist += 1; district_bremen_members -= 0.2

The shipyards of Hamburg and Wilhelmshaven stop for a day. It is not enough. On 4 February the troops take Bremen after a day of fighting. The strike has shown that Bremen was not alone, and that it was not enough.

@handover
subtitle: The Right's realism. Saves lives; the Bremen comrades will never forgive it.
on-arrival: bremen_line = 3; repression -= 2; district_bremen_loyalty -= 15; ultraleft_satisfaction -= 10; unionist_satisfaction += 6; lean_unionist += 2; lean_ultraleft -= 1

The Zentrale's courier tells the commissars that nobody is coming. Some of them want to negotiate; the rest want to fight. The troops enter Bremen on 4 February all the same. Fewer die than might have, and the Bremen radicals call the Zentrale cowards.
